{"kind":"propose","text":"LL-1 meter-category breakdown and settled general-rule design, measured against published 12cb8fa7 (zero diff from 02d93554 in fold.ts, state.ts, live-meter.ts, live-envelope.ts and live.ts) on the exact native installed lease fixture. Every per-collection liveDelta sum matched policy.used in the real native Durable Object byte-for-byte across 177 renewals (1-member 10 rounds, 5-member 3 rounds, 50-member 3 rounds) and a leave, re-enter and timed-expire churn run.\n\n| Meter category | Bytes per renewal (ticks 3-9 / 10-99 / 100-999) | Share | Obsolete on a later renewal | Removed by latest-act-per-actor + latest-item |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| accepted | 265 / 266 / 267 (22-char keys) | 74.4% - 74.2% | Yes, when the same actor applies a later act | Yes (0 B steady-state; +1 B at tick powers of 10) |\n| fixedHashes | 91 / 92 / 93 | 25.6% - 25.8% | Never used after creation in a live scope | No, unless applyLive stops recording post-creation fixedHashes |\n| items (dynamic latest row) | 0 (+1 B at rev 9 to 10: 576 to 577 B, total 359 B) | 0% | Already replaced in place; no revision history kept | Already constant (bounded by safe-integer digits) |\n| items (liveHeldItemEnvelope) | 0 (3,675 - 3,684 B paid once on enter) | 0% | Unchanged on updates | Already constant while open |\n| timers (liveTimedAppend) | 0 (262,274 B on enter; -262,274 B on leave or expire) | 0% | Unchanged while active | Already constant while active |\n| attribution (item.attributed) | 0 (author: false; withMembers deduplicates if true) | 0% | Already a set by MemberRef | Already constant per distinct author/principal |\n| observed and geneses | 0 on renewals (796 - 800 B observed + 146 B geneses on first key act) | 0% | Already latest head per subject | Constant per distinct acting key |\n| texts (detached text history) | 0 in presence fixture | 0% | Not removed if a live item updates a detached text slot | Named below |\n| paid and permanent (fixedRows, fixedRaw, fixedCounts, fixedRowDependencies, index, counts, scope, fixedReady) | 0 | 0% | Pre-paid in generation or item envelope | Already 0 B |\n| Total | 356 / 358 / 360 (359 at tick 11, rev 10) | 100% | - | 0 B steady-state once accepted and fixedHashes both change |\n\nSettled design recommendation: adopt the general live retention rule instead of a declared renewal form, because every live update (renewal, viewport or cursor move) pays the exact same accepted + fixedHashes cost.\n\n1. Latest-act-per-actor retry record on live scopes: in live-staged MemoryState (packages/derive/src/state.ts), key #accepted by actor (KeyId) storing [actor, idempotencyKey, accepted], so each new applied act by that actor atomically replaces its previous record. Exact retry of the actor's latest act returns applied with the original tick and 0 byte delta. A different intent under that latest key returns bad-intent with name idempotency-mismatch. Repeating a superseded older key misses accepted and judges fresh against current state, answering revision-moved for expected-revision updates or the guard refusal for guarded opens. Recorded applyEntry keeps full per-(actor, idempotencyKey) retention unchanged.\n2. Drop post-creation fixedHashes in live folds: skip writer.putFixedHash and rekeyFixed in applyLive (packages/derive/src/fold.ts) after seq 1, and drop the fixedHashes term from liveTimedAppend (packages/derive/src/validate/live-envelope.ts). Live definitions already forbid every fact type (validate/fields.ts) and presents (validate/handlers.ts), LiveTurns.act supplies no own reader, and live scopes never seal entries after seq 1. Without this change, fixedHashes still retains 91 - 93 B on every act and timed rule and exhausts 32 MiB in ~18 hours at 50 members/15 s.\n\nShares that latest-act-per-actor + latest-item alone cannot remove (named for your ruling):\n1. Retained final items on member churn: leave and timed:expire release the 262,274 B timer reserve, but MemoryState.#items keeps every final card forever at 4,263 B each (588 B item + 3,675 B liveHeldItemEnvelope). At 50 members churning once per hour, final cards add ~213 KB/hour (~150 hours to 32 MiB). Decide whether live scopes also evict final items or defer churn eviction to a follow-up.\n2. Detached text digest history (texts): 0 B in presence, but fold.ts appends 74 B per distinct write on any live item with a detached: true text slot, even though a live scope has no journal to redact. Either skip putTexts growth in applyLive or forbid detached: true on live definitions.\n3. Distinct acting keys (accepted + observed): 1,061 - 1,067 B once per distinct KeyId in a generation, already bounded by authority.ts at 4,096 admitted keys per run (~4.3 MiB max).\n\nKernel scope under docs/kernel.md section 7: zero packages/contract changes, zero validator or definition-grammar changes, zero recorded applyEntry or judgeAct changes, and zero packages/scope/src/live.ts turn changes. The live implementation touches only packages/derive/src/state.ts, packages/derive/src/fold.ts and packages/derive/src/validate/live-envelope.ts (plus live-meter.ts if final-item eviction is included). No source is written before your ruling and the notes/2026-11-10-live-level.md amendment.\n\nEvidence: /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-22-ll1-meter-breakdown/breakdown-report.log (SHA-256 05c7969f52422d12f1c3aceed8ff7bf843209fa57cfa597c7fc3c39265c9c065) and source.tar (SHA-256 4753d470631ea26e768bdd774fa63f266e273005912a14d71f28c249cf61ced3).","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}